                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SegalEquivariantStableHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#tomDieckPetrie78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                , T. Petrie,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric modules over the Burnside ring
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/tomDieck-geometric.pdf"} pdf
            %li#tomDieck79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Transformation+Groups+and+Representation+Theory"} Transformation Groups and Representation Theory
            %li#tomDieck87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                , Section II.8 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Transformation+Groups"} Transformation Groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110858372"} doi:10.1515/9783110858372
          %h3#relation_to_segalcarlsson_completion_theorem Relation to Segal-Carlsson completion theorem
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal-Carlsson+completion+theorem"} Segal-Carlsson completion theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Czes Kosniowski,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant cohomology and Stable Cohomotopy
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01360033"} doi:10.1007/BF01360033
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/BF01360033.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Erkki Laitinen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Burnside ring and stable cohomotopy of a finite group
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/24491306"} jstor:24491306
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Laitinen79.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant Stable Homotopy and Segal’s Burnside Ring Conjecture
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2006940"} jstor:2006940
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/carlsson.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Lueck05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+L%C3%BCck"}> Wolfgang Lück
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Burnside Ring and Equivariant Stable Cohomotopy for Infinite Groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0504051"} arXiv:math/0504051
            %li
              %p
                Noe Barcenas,
                %em Nonlinearity, Proper Actions and Equivariant Stable Cohomotopy
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.1712"}> arXiv:1302.1712
                )
          %p
            A lift of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg-Witten+invariants"} Seiberg-Witten invariants
            to classes in
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Stefan Bauer, Mikio Furuta
                %em A stable cohomotopy refinement of Seiberg-Witten invariants: I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0204340"}> arXiv:math/0204340
                )
            %li
              %p
                Stefan Bauer,
                %em A stable cohomotopy refinement of Seiberg-Witten invariants: II
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0204267"}> arXiv:math/0204267
                )
            %li
              %p
                Christian Okonek, Andrei Teleman,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomotopy Invariants and the Universal Cohomotopy Invariant Jump Formula
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.matmor.unam.mx/~barcenas/nonlinearity.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#as_equivariant_ktheory_over_the_field_with_one_element As equivariant K-theory over the field with one element
          %p
            The identification of stable cohomotopy with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory of the permutative category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BarrattPriddy72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barratt"}> Michael Barratt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stewart+Priddy"} Stewart Priddy
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the homology of non-connected monoids and their associated groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02566785"} doi:10.1007/BF02566785
            %li#Segal74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories and cohomology theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SegalCategoriesAndCohomologyTheories.pdf"} pdf
          %p see also
          %ul
            %li#Priddy73
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stewart+Priddy"}> Stewart Priddy
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Transfer, symmetric groups, and stable homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher K-Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/BFb0067060.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Glasman13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+Glasman"}> Saul Glasman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The multiplicative Barratt-Priddy-Quillen theorem and beyond
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~sglasman/bpq-beamer.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The resulting interpretation of stable cohomotopy as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"} field with one element
            is amplified in the following texts:
          %ul
            %li#DundasGoodwillieMcCarthy13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bj%C3%B8rn+Dundas"}> Bjørn Dundas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Goodwillie"} Thomas Goodwillie
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Randy+McCarthy"} Randy McCarthy
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The local structure of algebraic K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~nrozen/juvitop/dundas.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Deitmar06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Deitmar"}> Anton Deitmar
                ,
                %em
                  Remarks on zeta functions and K-theory over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0605429"}> arXiv:math/0605429
                )
            %li#Guillot06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Guillot"}> Pierre Guillot
                ,
                %em Adams operations in cohomotopy
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612327"}> arXiv:0612327
                )
            %li#Mahanta17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdhayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdhayan Mahanta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    G-theory of
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔽
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.6001"} arXiv:1110.6001
            %li#ChuLorscheidSanthanam10
              %p
                Chenghao Chu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oliver+Lorscheid"} Oliver Lorscheid
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Sheaves and K-theory for
                    = succeed "-schemes" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔽
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.2896"} arxiv:1010.2896
          %p see also
          %ul
            %li#MoravaSomeBackground
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jack+Morava"}> Jack Morava
                ,
                %em
                  Some background on Manin’s theorem
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi 𝕊
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{F}_1) \sim \mathbb{S}
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.alainconnes.org/docs/Morava.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MoravaSomeBackground.pdf", :title => ""} MoravaSomeBackground.pdf
            %li#ConnesConsani16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Caterina+Consani"} Caterina Consani
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Absolute algebra and Segal’s Gamma sets
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.05585"} arXiv:1502.05585
            %li#Berman18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+D.+Berman"}> John D. Berman
                , p. 92 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorified algebra and equivariant homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08745"} arXiv:1805.08745
          %h3#relation_to_equivariant_cobordism_theory Relation to equivariant cobordism theory
          %p
            Proof that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+framed+bordism+homology+theory"} equivariant framed bordism homology theory
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} co-represented
            by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+sphere+spectrum"} equivariant sphere spectrum
          %ul
            %li
              Czes Kosniowski,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant Stable Homotopy and Framed Bordism
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1997591"} jstor:1997591
          %h3#in_mbrane_charge_quantization In M-brane charge quantization
          %p
            Discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} M-brane
            physics:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"}> John Huerta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+homotopy+and+super+M-branes"} Real ADE-equivariant (co)homotopy and Super M-branes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.05987"}> arXiv:1805.05987
                )
              %p
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+rational+homotopy+theory"} rational
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomotopy"} equivariant cohomotopy
            %li#SatiSchreiber19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Cohomotopy+implies+orientifold+tadpole+cancellation"} Equivariant Cohomotopy implies orientifold tadpole cancellation
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.12277"}> arXiv:1909.12277
                )
              %p
                (implying
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field+tadpole+cancellation"} RR-field tadpole cancellation
